            <ArticleTitle>Is coronary artery surgery so expensive?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>570-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Severe angina may lead to complete invalidism, with reliance on social security payments and accumulated savings. The average cost of this situation to the patient is $4-6000 pa and to the State $3-4000 pa. Reputedly expensive cardiac operations are cheaper, at under $2000, than unoperated invalidism, and thus rapidly repay their cost in addition to their non-financial attributes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
